            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>For Krishnamurthy, who is on eight medications from three specialists, which tool should the team use to identify medications that are potentially inappropriate for his age, or being wrongly withheld?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Charlson Comorbidity Index</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The Charlson Comorbidity Index predicts mortality risk from comorbid conditions; it does not evaluate medication appropriateness.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Beers Criteria and STOPP/START criteria</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Beers Criteria flags potentially inappropriate medications for older adults, while STOPP/START also catches medications wrongly omitted — together they guide the simplest effective regimen for a patient like Krishnamurthy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Confusion Assessment Method</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CAM screens for delirium, not for medication appropriateness.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mini Nutritional Assessment short form</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>The MNA-SF screens for malnutrition risk, not polypharmacy issues.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
